cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Loopwise in work you publish, please cite it."
title: "Loopwise: active-learning experiment selection for small-n biological assays"
abstract: >-
  Loopwise implements and compares batch-selection policies for iterative
  experimental campaigns in which a model proposes candidates, a small number
  can be measured per round, and the measurements retrain the model. It spans
  greedy exploitation through information-seeking selection (BALD, expected
  model change, Thompson sampling) and batch-diversity constraints (facility
  location, k-DPP), and adds the plate-level realism such campaigns require:
  96- and 384-well layout with reserved controls, edge-effect-aware
  randomization, per-compound and per-plate cost models, and replicate
  policies. A retrospective replay harness evaluates every policy on fully
  measured public datasets, reporting cumulative hits, held-out model quality
  and rounds-to-target.
type: software
authors:
